    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1129">

                <pb facs="1026" n="712" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg712"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Liberia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Buckner</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-07">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 7, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Strongly recommend to Liberian Government that President issue neutrality
                    proclamation at once if he has not already done so.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1129-f1"/> Department has asked British, French, and German
                    Governments to give assurance that neutrality of Liberia will be respected.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1129-f1" n="2" xml:id="d1129-f1-content">
                <p>The proclamation was issued August 10, 1914 (File No. 763.72111N39/21).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
